Implement DADAO memory instructions (DG-004b), spec-derived (§2.1 big-endian,
§3.1-§3.4 RD load/store/multi, §4.1/§4.2/§4.5/§4.6 RB variants):

  - RD single load  ldbs/ldbu/ldws/ldwu/ldts/ldtu/ldo  (op 0x30-0x33,0x40-0x42)
  - RD single store stb/stw/stt/sto                     (op 0x38-0x3B)
  - RD multi  load  ldm{bs,bu,ws,wu,ts,tu,o}            (op 0x34-0x37,0x44-0x46)
  - RD multi  store stm{b,w,t,o}                        (op 0x3C-0x3F)
  - RB load/store   ldo-rb/sto-rb, ldmo-rb/stmo-rb      (op 0x43,0x4B,0x47,0x4F)
  - RB wyde imm     setzw-rb/orw-rb/andnw-rb            (op 0x4E,0x4C,0x4D)
  - RB compare      cmp-rb (fixes 0x2D: was comparing RD, now RB 48-bit §4.5)

EA = (rbhb[47:0] + off) mod 2^48 (§1.3); multi EA_i adds rdhc + i*N (§3.3).
All multi-byte accesses assemble/disassemble bytes explicitly big-endian, so
host endianness is irrelevant. Atomic readMem/writeMem via ExecContext.

Harness plumbing:
  - dadao_se.py: switch to AtomicSimpleCPU (synchronous readMem/writeMem;
    multi-element loops need no timing split). Smokes unchanged (42/42/0).
  - decoder.cc dumpFinalState: at halt, tryReadBlob a fixed memory window
    [0x87FEF000,+0x3000) and emit DADAO_MEMDUMP for the differential adapter;
    tryReadBlob so smoke ELFs (window unmapped) do not abort.
  - gen_min_elf.build_elf: optional RW data segments (the adapter maps the
    memory window so loads/stores have valid pages + initial contents).

Exceptions/faults (ILLI/MALIGN/store-from-rd0/immu6=0) deferred to DG-004c;
those vectors remain gem5-SKIP.

3-way differential: AGREE(3-way) 77 -> 131, DIVERGE=0.
rd-load-store PASS=38/SKIP=11/FAIL=0; rb-ops PASS=20/SKIP=8/FAIL=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
